# time() with a zone, from the softcode audit (#2268): UTC, a whole number of hours and a fractional one
# are zones, and anything that is neither a zone nor an object is an invalid time zone.
::case time.login
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
think ok

::case time.zone  time() reads UTC and numeric offsets as zones
think [lte(abs(sub(convtime(time(utc),UTC),secs())),2)]
think [lte(abs(add(sub(convtime(time(-8),UTC),convtime(time(utc),UTC)),28800)),2)]
think [lte(abs(sub(sub(convtime(time(5.5),UTC),convtime(time(utc),UTC)),19800)),2)]
think [time(Nowhere/Atlantis)]
think [time(24)]

::case time.mtime  an attribute or lock write moves mtime past ctime; a clone keeps its original's
# atr_add (src/attrib.c) and do_lock (src/lock.c) set ModTime(thing) = mudtime; do_clone copies the
# original's (src/create.c:653-655). The waits put the write at least a second after the creation.
@create MtimeAttr
::until MTIMEATTR
@wait 2={&COLOUR MtimeAttr=red;think [gt(msecs(MtimeAttr),csecs(MtimeAttr))] MTIMEATTR}
@create MtimeLock
::until MTIMELOCK
@wait 2={@lock MtimeLock=me;think [gt(msecs(MtimeLock),csecs(MtimeLock))] MTIMELOCK}
@clone MtimeAttr=MtimeCopy
think [eq(msecs(MtimeCopy),msecs(MtimeAttr))] [lt(msecs(MtimeCopy),csecs(MtimeCopy))]
@recycle MtimeCopy
@recycle MtimeLock
@recycle MtimeAttr
